    {
      "id": "01",
      "title": "The page fault",
      "question": "What happens when a program touches a page that isn't in memory?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Page faults, question one. A program touches a page that isn't in memory right now. What happens, step by step? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "Touch a page that isn't <em>in memory</em>. Then what?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Every load or store is translated. If the page table entry says not present, the CPU raises a page fault, and the kernel takes over. First: is the address inside any mapping the process owns? If not, it's a bug, and the process gets a segmentation fault. If it is, the kernel finds a free frame, evicting another page if memory is full. If the data lives on disk, in swap or in a mapped file, the kernel starts the read, and the process blocks, so another one runs. When the data arrives, the kernel marks the entry present, and retries the faulting instruction. It succeeds, as if nothing happened.",
          "props": {
            "title": "The <em>fault</em> path",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "acc",
                "label": "load / store",
                "x": 230,
                "y": 290,
                "w": 260,
                "h": 80
              },
              {
                "id": "pte",
                "label": "PTE: present = 0",
                "x": 590,
                "y": 290,
                "w": 300,
                "h": 80
              },
              {
                "id": "trap",
                "label": "page fault\n→ kernel",
                "x": 950,
                "y": 290,
                "w": 260,
                "h": 96,
                "hidden": true
              },
              {
                "id": "segv",
                "label": "not in any mapping\n→ SIGSEGV",
                "x": 950,
                "y": 480,
                "w": 320,
                "h": 96,
                "hidden": true
              },
              {
                "id": "frame",
